## Interpretation

The main latency contributor is ASR. Signal detection and nudge generation are lightweight because the prototype uses deterministic rule-based detection.

The measured end-to-end P95 latency was approximately 1.37 seconds for a 5-second audio chunk.

## Limitations

The current prototype runs Faster-Whisper locally on CPU. Production deployment could reduce latency further using GPU inference, optimized ASR models, streaming ASR, batching where appropriate, and lower-latency inference infrastructure.

The current prototype also uses 5-second chunks, so signal availability is affected by chunk duration.

The transcript can contain minor chunk-boundary artifacts because each chunk is transcribed independently.

## Production Considerations

At higher scale, latency should be monitored continuously and the ASR component should be optimized independently from the signal and nudge layers.

A production implementation should also support speaker diarization so that agent and customer statements can be distinguished before generating alerts.